[{:db/id "q-15647/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "ef55e054-3b41-52ee-aef5-22ac31bec600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15647/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "9e06efb1-c614-5df4-a96d-54a8bc3e08a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15647/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "286f6836-e5cf-5ad9-91af-0d37c393b681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15647/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "8494c0c2-11ad-5038-8e44-e8984fcbc27b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15647/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "34f74688-ce7b-5d2e-ac6b-ba72b6e3921a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15647/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3af8268c-56b5-5e72-85f4-2e16fa02fce9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15647/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-15647/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-15647/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-15647/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-15647/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-15647/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15647" :question/id #uuid "0c36b197-027f-56c2-a704-60e8c33c39b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-15647" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{3x+1}$ and the point $P(21,4)$ that lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is invertible in the vicinity of $P,$ calculate ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4).$" :question/worked-solution "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(21,4).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\sqrt[3]{3x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{2/3}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(21) & =\\frac{1}{(64)^{2/3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(21,4)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(4,21)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$ \n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(21)} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15647/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e05385-7cb6-5f21-b0d8-a7641d912d5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15647"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342588/field-1/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" :answer/id #uuid "abf62472-d96a-5ca8-866a-dad158af934e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342588/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "b91cc901-d4a8-5750-bee2-35b539bb8889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342588/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1a287c1-3c09-5131-a2d0-07ea90edf310" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342588/field-1/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" :answer-field/choices ["q-342588/field-1/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" "q-342588/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342588" :question/id #uuid "284514bc-fbdd-5962-b8a5-481ef5bc2a15" :question/math-academy-id "q-342588" :question/problem "Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(1)$ given the following table of values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $-2$ | $4$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $-7$ |\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(1))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(1)=2$ and ${f}^{′}(2)=-7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(1))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-7)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342588/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b492068c-2bd2-5611-baab-780959d24c3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342588"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342592/field-1/aa640bdf1bd5b2b15c3dbfe770f68b41d304d610e4d1af786c1f1372fe3dc48f" :answer/id #uuid "93d6c80e-e791-55aa-b703-f982b38ee085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342592/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d62851f2-84e2-56c0-8a05-177da63414c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342592/field-1/aa640bdf1bd5b2b15c3dbfe770f68b41d304d610e4d1af786c1f1372fe3dc48f" :answer-field/choices ["q-342592/field-1/aa640bdf1bd5b2b15c3dbfe770f68b41d304d610e4d1af786c1f1372fe3dc48f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342592" :question/id #uuid "f0036795-b710-5f8f-94db-babdb3b4d3c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-342592" :question/problem "Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)$ given the following table of values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $-8$ |\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(0)=2$ and ${f}^{′}(2)=-8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-8)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342592/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b492068c-2bd2-5611-baab-780959d24c3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342592"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342624/field-1/0f07028be0129224d3b47e78608cd8d21e539f8150e14564a66a4130dd7bc14e" :answer/id #uuid "f5809f2a-705f-56ad-89df-26eff0e73638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln(5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342624/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "9d4899d4-2b6e-5d3b-af50-d9fb3cd450ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342624/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "933a8f66-b4f5-56c5-9264-4e3259c3756c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342624/field-1/0f07028be0129224d3b47e78608cd8d21e539f8150e14564a66a4130dd7bc14e" :answer-field/choices ["q-342624/field-1/0f07028be0129224d3b47e78608cd8d21e539f8150e14564a66a4130dd7bc14e" "q-342624/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342624" :question/id #uuid "03828b42-335e-5615-88ca-ef552635348d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342624" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={5}^{x}+3.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4).$\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(4).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(4)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(4) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =4 \\\\ {5}^{x}+3 & =4 \\\\ {5}^{x} & =1 \\\\ {5}^{x} & ={5}^{0} \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(4)=0.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={5}^{x}+3 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & ={5}^{0}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342624/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b2a80aa-7882-50eb-bfe0-c0eeab72161d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342624"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342625/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "5a8647fa-d56d-55e8-86fd-f6210ac630a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342625/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a93944aa-d827-5aa6-bd4d-ad8afdb1f5ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342625/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer-field/choices ["q-342625/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342625" :question/id #uuid "77a5f47e-8f48-52c6-b3b5-dcc98f89fccd" :question/math-academy-id "q-342625" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=(x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1).$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0).$\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(0).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(0)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(0) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =0 \\\\ (x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(0)=2.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1) \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)+\\frac{x+3}{x-1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-1)+\\frac{2+3}{2-1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =0+5 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-342625/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b2a80aa-7882-50eb-bfe0-c0eeab72161d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342625"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
